{% load static %}
<main id="home-page"
      class="home-page"
      data-default-name="{{ data.default_name }}">
  <h1>It works</h1>
  <p>
    This is <code>HomePage</code>, in <code>pages/home_page/</code>. Its controller,
    <code>home_page.ts</code>, fills the name in from a <code>data-</code> attribute,
    calls <code>GreetingEndpoint</code> at the URL <code>AppUrls</code> holds, and
    shows the answer with the site name from <code>AppState</code>.
  </p>
  <form id="home-page__greeting-form"
        class="home-page__greeting-form">
    <label>
      Name
      <input id="home-page__name-input"
             type="text">
    </label>
    <button type="submit">Ask the server</button>
    <loading-spinner id="home-page__spinner"
                     hidden>
    </loading-spinner>
  </form>
  <p id="home-page__greeting"></p>
  <p>
    <a href="{% url '__app_label__:ForbiddenExamplePage' %}">A page that is always refused</a>
  </p>

  <h2>Next steps</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Add a page: <code>python manage.py ww_create_page about_page</code></li>
    <li>Add a widget: <code>python manage.py ww_create_widget info_card</code></li>
    <li>Check the setup: <code>python manage.py ww_doctor</code></li>
    <li>
      Read how it all works: <code>__app_label__/website_widgets_docs/AGENTS.md</code>, or the
      <a href="https://github.com/nateonguitar/django-website-widgets#readme">README</a>
    </li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Example apps</h2>
  <p>
    Small runnable projects, each showing one part of the package
    (<a href="https://github.com/nateonguitar/django-website-widgets/tree/main/examples">all of them</a>):
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li>
      <a href="https://github.com/nateonguitar/django-website-widgets/tree/main/examples/slim/01_pages_and_widgets">Pages and widgets</a>:
      child widgets, variant templates, and the async ORM in a page
    </li>
    <li>
      <a href="https://github.com/nateonguitar/django-website-widgets/tree/main/examples/slim/02_requests_and_routing">Requests and routing</a>:
      routing, 401, 403 and 404 pages, redirects, and a "load more" endpoint
    </li>
    <li>
      <a href="https://github.com/nateonguitar/django-website-widgets/tree/main/examples/slim/03_widgets_in_plain_django">Widgets in plain Django</a>:
      widgets in an ordinary view, HTML emails, and an admin page
    </li>
    <li>
      <a href="https://github.com/nateonguitar/django-website-widgets/tree/main/examples/slim/04_project_tracker">Project tracker</a>:
      a small working app with sign-in and JSON endpoints
    </li>
  </ul>
</main>

<script type="module">
  import { HomePageController } from '{% static "main.js" %}';
  HomePageController.initializeController();
</script>
